## Migration from Lwt/Async to Eio

### Concurrent operations

**Before (Lwt):**
```ocaml
let%lwt result1 = fetch_data1 () in
let%lwt result2 = fetch_data2 () in
Lwt.return (result1 + result2)

(* Or parallel: *)
let%lwt result1, result2 = Lwt.both (fetch_data1 ()) (fetch_data2 ()) in
Lwt.return (result1 + result2)
```

**After (Eio):**
```ocaml
(* Sequential *)
let result1 = fetch_data1 () in
let result2 = fetch_data2 () in
result1 + result2

(* Parallel with fibers *)
Eio.Fiber.both
  (fun () -> fetch_data1 ())
  (fun () -> fetch_data2 ())
|> fun (result1, result2) -> result1 + result2
```

### Error handling

**Before (Lwt):**
```ocaml
Lwt.catch
  (fun () -> send_message ~chat_id ~text)
  (function
   | Api_error msg -> handle_error msg
   | exn -> Lwt.fail exn)
```

**After (Eio with Result):**
```ocaml
match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text () with
| Ok message -> (* success *)
| Error err ->
    match err with
    | Telegram.Error.Api_error { error_code; description; _ } ->
        (* Handle specific error *)
    | _ -> (* Handle other errors *)
```

### Streaming and backpressure

**Before (Lwt_stream):**
```ocaml
let stream = Lwt_stream.from (fun () ->
  match%lwt get_update () with
  | Some update -> Lwt.return (Some update)
  | None -> Lwt.return None
) in
Lwt_stream.iter_s process_update stream
```

**After (Eio):**
```ocaml
(* Eio handles backpressure naturally with structured concurrency *)
Tg.Polling.run client ~handler:(fun update ->
  (* Process update - backpressure is automatic *)
  process_update update
)
```

### Timeouts

**Before (Lwt):**
```ocaml
Lwt.pick [
  send_message ~chat_id ~text;
  Lwt_unix.sleep 5.0 >>= fun () -> Lwt.fail Timeout
]
```

**After (Eio):**
```ocaml
(* Set timeout when creating client *)
let client = Telegram.Client.create ~env ~token
  ~http_timeout:(Some 5.0) () in

(* Or use Eio's timeout primitives *)
Eio.Time.with_timeout clock 5.0
  (fun () -> Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ())
```

