## Migration from synchronous OCaml code

### Basic I/O

**Before (blocking):**
```ocaml
let content = In_channel.read_all "file.txt" in
let response = Http_client.post ~body:content url in
print_endline response
```

**After (Eio):**
```ocaml
Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  let fs = Eio.Stdenv.fs env in
  let content = Eio.Path.(load (fs / "file.txt")) in

  let client = Telegram.Client.create ~env ~token () in
  match Gen_methods.send_document client ~chat_id ~document:content () with
  | Ok _ -> Eio.traceln "Sent!"
  | Error e -> Eio.traceln "Error: %a" Telegram.Error.pp e
```

### File uploads

**Before:**
```ocaml
let ch = open_in_bin "photo.jpg" in
let data = really_input_string ch (in_channel_length ch) in
close_in ch;
send_photo ~chat_id ~photo:data
```

**After:**
```ocaml
(* Direct path - streaming upload *)
Gen_methods.send_photo client ~chat_id ~photo:"photo.jpg" ()

(* Or with explicit file handling *)
Eio.Path.with_open_in (fs / "photo.jpg") @@ fun file ->
  Gen_methods.send_photo client ~chat_id ~photo:"photo.jpg" ()
```

